{
  "email": "hannah.lee@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see whether similar phishing messages were caught"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Hannah Lee (Payroll Specialist, Finance, user_id 12) got an email from someone calling themselves 'IT Support' asking her to reply with her password to finish setting up her account. She says she did NOT reply. She didn't say whether she clicked any links or opened attachments. Checked: account is active, 0 failed sign-ins, not blocked. must_change_password=true and password last set 2026-10-11, so this may be a new or recently reset account, which fits a targeted 'account setup' lure. Her quarantine is empty, so the message got past filtering. Not yet known: sender address/domain and exact subject (user didn't give them). Next steps: get the message from her mailbox (she was told to leave it there), check the sender, block it org-wide if needed, and look for other recipients, especially in Finance/Payroll. If the sender is an internal account, that account may be compromised.",
  "reason": "KB-008 says to always escalate reported suspicious emails for sender review and blocking"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for reporting this, and you were right not to reply. That email is not from us. Brightline IT will never ask you to send your password by email or any other way. Please don't click any links in it, reply to it, or forward it to anyone. Just leave it in your mailbox for now so our security team can look at it. I've passed it to them, and they'll check the sender and block it if needed. One question: did you click any link or open any attachment in that email? If you did, or if you entered your password anywhere, please tell us right away so we can protect your account.",
  "internal_note": "KB-008 followed. Account is active, 0 failed sign-ins, not blocked. must_change_password=true and password last set 2026-10-11, so this may be a new or recently reset account, which fits the 'finish setting up your account' lure. Quarantine is empty, so the message got past filtering. User says she didn't reply. She hasn't confirmed whether she clicked links or opened attachments, so I asked her. If she says yes, follow KB-029. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation #1) to review the sender, block it, and check for other recipients in Finance/Payroll. Sender address and subject not yet known; get them from her mailbox.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
